Guys, you understand it is a proof language, not an app, right? No, we cannot launch it and fix it later. Once there are thousands of libraries written by many users, there's no going back. If we launch with some fundamental mistake on the core, it will be with us forever or be very hard to rollback.

JavaScript has to deal with eval() forever, and even smaller languages like Agda had to make a huge effort to eliminate bad decisions, such as the K axiom, which was accidental. Just chill, it will be done when it is done.

